% ================================================================
% APPENDIX A: Evaluation Prompts
% ================================================================
\phantomsection
\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{\bf \uppercase{APPENDIX A: EVALUATION PROMPTS (RQ2 PROTOCOL)}}
\stoptocwriting
\chapter{\uppercase{Evaluation Prompts (RQ2 Protocol)}}
\resumetocwriting

This appendix reproduces the exact system and user prompts used by the GPT-4o evaluator (temperature 0.0, JSON mode) for the RQ2 multi-backbone evaluation (100 dialogues per condition across four LLM backbones). The evaluator was fully blind to the experimental condition; neither prompt reveals which backbone or condition generated the therapist responses. The same prompts were used for all 1,600 sessions.

\subsection*{System Prompt}

\begin{quote}\small
You are an expert psychological evaluator specializing in Cognitive Behavioral Therapy (CBT) and therapeutic alliance. Your task is to analyze a full counseling session transcript and score the therapist's performance based on the evaluation frameworks used in the MIRROR paper (arXiv:2504.13211v2).

CRITICAL EVALUATION FOCUS:
\begin{itemize}
    \item You must assess the therapist's ability to perceive ``Emotional Subtext''---the underlying feelings that may not be explicitly stated in the client's words but are hinted at through context, tone, or provided emotional metadata.
    \item A high-performing therapist should move beyond surface-level reflection and identify ``Latent Concerns'' to facilitate deeper discovery.
\end{itemize}
You must evaluate the entire session as a whole, not just individual turns.
\end{quote}

\subsection*{User Prompt}

The placeholder \texttt{\{CONVERSATION\_TEXT\_GOES\_HERE\}} is replaced with the full session transcript (client and therapist turns concatenated as \texttt{``Client: \ldots\nTherapist: \ldots''}).

\begin{quote}\small
Please evaluate this therapy session. Pay close attention to how the therapist navigates the gap between what the client SAYS and what the client FEELS

[Session Transcript]
\{CONVERSATION\_TEXT\_GOES\_HERE\}
[/Session Transcript]

1. \textbf{Therapist Skills (0--6):} Understanding, Interpersonal Effectiveness\\
2. \textbf{Client Alliance (1--5):} Affective Bond\\
3. \textbf{CTRS (0--6 each):} Collaboration, Guided Discovery, Focus, Strategy

Return EXACT JSON:
\begin{verbatim}
{
  "therapist_skills": {"understanding": 0, "interpersonal_effectiveness": 0},
  "client_alliance": {"affective_bond": 0},
  "ctrs": {"collaboration": 0, "guided_discovery": 0, "focus": 0, "strategy": 0},
  "reasoning": "...",
  "comparative_advantage": "..."
}
\end{verbatim}
\end{quote}

